<title>FRANCE: France sells 18.59 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 18.59 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury sold the following government bonds (BTANs) at auction on Thursday.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.OCT.98	4.50	  9.985 BLN	  3.50</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 24.285 BLN/2.4		  135 MLN	   101.67</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 100.0						   06.JAN</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.OCT.01	5.50	  8.600 BLN	  4.70</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 17.850 BLN/2.1		   350 MLN	   103.30</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 100.0						   13.JAN</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT OFFER</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 17 to 19 billion francs of BTANs in total today. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 2.3.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
